1
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Off the map, things get strange.

2
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Encounters at the End of the World is a
documentary film directed by Werner Herzog.

3
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Herzog and cinematographer Peter Zeitlinger go to Antarctica to meet people who live and
work there, and to capture footage of the continent's unique locations.

4
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Herzog's voiceover narration explains that his film will not be a typical Antarctica film about
"fluffy penguins", but will explore the dreams of the people and the landscape.

5
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Narrator (voice), played by Werner Herzog.

6
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
Self - Volcanologist, played by Clive Oppenheimer.

7
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:18,000
Self - Transportation Dept, played by Scott Rowland.

8
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Self - Philosopher, Forklift Driver, played by Stefan Pashov.

9
00:59:24,000 --> 00:59:30,000
Self - Glaciologist, played by Doug MacAyeal.

10
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Self - Filmmaker, Cook, played by Ryan Andrew Evans.

11
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:42,000
Encounters at the End of the World is a 2007 American documentary film by Werner
Herzog about Antarctica and the people who choose to spend time there.

12
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
It was released in North America on June 11, 2008, and distributed by ThinkFilm.

13
01:25:48,000 --> 01:25:54,000
At the 81st Academy Awards, the film was nominated for Best Documentary Feature.

14
01:32:24,000 --> 01:32:30,000
The film explores themes of marine biologist,
penguin, iceberg, volcano, wilderness.
